[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（英音）]
[ti:A Glass Envelope]
[00:13.43]How did Jane receive a letter from a stranger?
[00:20.26]My daughter, Jane, never dreamed of receiving a letter from a girl of her own age in Holland.
[00:29.79]Last year, we were travelling across the Channel and Jane put a piece of paper with her name and address on it into a bottle.
[00:41.38]She threw the bottle into the sea.
[00:45.82]She never thought of it again, but ten months later, she received a letter from a girl in Holland.
[00:55.36]Both girls write to each other regularly now.
[00:59.71]However, they have decided to use the post office.
[01:04.41]Letters will cost a little more, but they will certainly travel faster.
